From 0fbed244f61108bb368972cea518daf6429a4495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 09:23:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the requested RoCE collective policy explicit and
 fail-stop

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354, after the
spark3 vLLM 0001-0026 series. Requires B12X dispatch-capacity support.

Report dispatch and registered capacity independently from the live runtime.
Keep sequence-parallel prefill on its qualified capacity floor. Treat
multi-node RoCE selection as a required RoCE/PyNCCL policy: startup errors
abort, and ineligible operations go directly to PyNCCL without trying other
accelerators or the PyTorch process-group fallback.

Quality: no numerical kernel or size boundary changes in the selected arm.
Single-node and non-RoCE groups retain the general upstream dispatch chain.
Tests: CPU execution of extracted adapter/runtime predicates and dispatcher
methods covers boundaries, logs, backend failures and the 205-token SP floor.
GPU build/serving qualification remains required before deployment.
Upstream status: local experimental patch, not submitted.
